    "title": "test(mem): add retained native context provider fixture",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T05:35:05Z",
    "body": "## Problem\n\nThe existing F2 regressions qualify the original episodic writer, source freshness and explicit-context restrictions. They do not yet join that fixture to a real provider through the actual durable native driver. This draft makes one narrow, opt-in path observation reviewable without enabling it in ordinary test runs.\n\n## Change\n\nAdd one ignored Linux-only case under the existing private production-composition fixture. It imports one freshly generated private fact through the original retained writer and source verifier, starts the F2 ExplicitContextOnly App Server, and calls the real AppServerModelDriver with a DurableInferenceControl journal and one explicitly fixture-only Unix final-use claim.\n\nThe nonce is absent from prompts, query values, filenames, config and expected-answer files before dispatch. Success requires the real returned value, two source checks before the claim and two after, the original durable thread/turn terminal and context/authority correlation, an unchanged canonical owner cut and no original fixture outbox dispatch. The existing native client identity retains its deny-only empty tool router.\n\nKeep the original 0700 fixture directory and native journal before any provider start. Record actual outcomes before success checks; unknown acknowledgements retain their original identity and never cause a fresh request retry. Only this case's own tasks are stopped. The fixture signer uses an existing public test-key pattern and is not a deployment credential or independent source owner.\n\n## Source and native validation\n\n- Parent: `0c32926cfec58d986477fc72ba3a4787ab75fde9`; new source: `9d9bdfbaeeec3c618f3fc80e2f663a29c13f4b27`; tree: `07192603a5164f4b5d4da24e37595be2a0a04777`.\n- Exactly four test-only paths, +618/-1. No Cargo dependency or production authority API change.\n- Actual repository `just fmt` with Rust 1.96.0 / rustfmt 1.9.0 / just 1.51.0 completed in a separate clone of clean F2. Only the two new files were formatted; no out-of-scope source changed; the donor remained clean.\n- Complete original formatter archive: 41,624 bytes, SHA256 `d2fee84f30985c162ef778c9956c033c74f252bef8be5a7c03ae84c290056c14`. All 43 members, 34 artifact hashes and 26 raw step logs were independently read back; the final patch replays to all four exact postimages.\n- All four published source blobs were fully read back and match those actual formatter postimages. Independent final static review found no must-fix; it is not a compile result.\n- Independent zero-model native run `mem8-native-g-9d9bdfb-ai395-20261111-ed353-v1` passed on this exact source/tree. It started at 2026-11-11 05:18:34.833360 UTC and finished at 05:26:34.961045 UTC, before its separately fixed 06:03:34.833360 UTC deadline.\n- Actual nextest result: **6 passed, 0 failed, 782 skipped**. All six fully qualified names match the predeclared existing F2 control set; the actual commit, revoke and panic child markers are present. The ignored real-provider case was not selected or executed; its enabling provider/context/source-SHA variables were removed. No result from the old F campaign was imported.\n- A fresh `cargo build --locked -p codex-cli --bin codex` on this G checkout bound the real executable via `CARGO_BIN_EXE_codex`. Observed binary: 559,365,856 bytes, SHA256 `49bfbb583bc08a549f8f023880875d2541473f5ec9b3ddd613298855fdf3e976`, identical before/after the tests and fix. Its bytes also match F2 because this patch changes only test code; the new build/source receipts were independently recorded.\n- Repository `just fmt --base 0c32926cfec58d986477fc72ba3a4787ab75fde9`, V8 input resolution, the CLI build, six controls and `just fix --locked -p codex-hepta-agentd` all completed on clean exact G HEAD/tree. Source and index rewrite patches are both empty; the four source-file bytes match the published formatter postimages; the F2 donor remained clean.\n- Complete original native archive: **67 files, 49,292 bytes**, SHA256 `3babe551f6a029803467dbc89f5ea949c88b93916bb20c3638bb5ba276b50a75`, Git blob `887bd1823ce74a0e579dac39deae6bd9a77fae8c`. The complete archive/receipts/log hashes, six named passes, three actual markers, source bytes and binary metadata were independently read back. Audit blob: `712f89d3b78a32bc101a2b8fcca3947611f7794e`; exact source-tar audit: `f09151dd7f4e6826e7c3d8dd8d48c9ca8108869b`.\n- This qualifies compilation and the six existing controls on G. It does not execute the new provider-memory path, adjudicate every repository CI gate, or permit merging this draft.\n\n## Boundaries\n\nNo G provider request has been issued. The existing ordinary provider smoke's unresolved original turn must be reconciled separately; this new fixture must not replay or replace it. No provider call is authorized by this draft or its zero-model regression phase.\n\nEven a later successful opt-in case would establish only one synthetic fresh-thread context path. The physical provider payload/request count, remote model identity, unseen-source benefit, complete original deployment recovery and independent trust/effect owners remain unverified. Scientific acceptance stays HOLD. F2 and its completed campaign are unchanged.",
